# Prompt switches, off by default, on top of 0124 and 0125. None changes a bit of any reply (four Sparks cabled as a
# ring, 2026-10-21: five solo greedy prompts of 5K-13K tokens, identical replies with and without; prx is a transport).
#
# TF_GLM_PROMPT_HANDOFF8=1 (with TF_GLM_PROMPT_W8): before a KDA layer a micro-batched chunk's glue rounds this rank's
#   normed rows to e4m3 once and swaps those and their scales (half the bytes) instead of the bf16 rows; the KDA
#   projection reads them. After RiNGSiDE's KDA FP8 handoff. +2.5-3 % prompt.
# TF_GLM_PRX=1 (four Sparks cabled as a ring): the row split's exchanges moved by the NICs alone (cuda/prx.py,
#   cuda/prx_proxy.c): the copy engines stage each peer's bytes in a pinned region, a proxy thread RDMA-writes them to
#   both neighbours over both PCIe functions of the cable, the neighbours' proxies relay the across rank's halves, the
#   GPU waits with stream memory operations; no NCCL kernel and no SM. +9-13 % prompt.
# TF_GLM_PRX_SHARE=1: a second channel and stream for the DSA layers' own-row shares (+4 % at 8K).
#   TF_GLM_PRX_RINGAG=1: an all-gather's across halves relayed from the block the neighbour received (3 blocks on the
#   wire a rank, not 4; +0.3-1.7 %). TF_GLM_PRX_ZC=1: the partials written into the send slots and summed where they
#   land (no staging copies; +2-2.5 %).
# prx costs ~770 MiB of pinned host memory a rank and a CPU core a channel while it polls (patch 0127: it sleeps when
#   idle). It needs a RoCE v2 IPv4 GID on each of a rank's first four NCCL_IB_HCA devices (or TF_GLM_PRX_HCA). A
#   failed RDMA write or a dead peer leaves the GPU waiting on a flag: the host raises at its next exchange call
#   (patch 0127 bounds this).
#
# Provenance and credit: the KDA FP8 handoff and the two-way relay round the ring follow RiNGSiDE's prefill ring
# (othexmr/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4-2x-4x-DGX-Sparks-RiNGSiDE, Apache License 2.0); prx_proxy.c's verbs setup follows
# b12x's roce_proxy.c (Apache License 2.0). No code of either is copied beyond the verbs calls' shape.

